.TH CHOWN 3crunch "" "Crunch" "Crunch Library Manual"
.SH NAME
chown \- change a file's ownership
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B #include <unistd.h>
.B int chown(const char* path, uid_t owner, gid_t group);
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
Changes the owner and group of path, following symbolic links.  Either ID may
be (uid_t)\-1 or (gid_t)\-1 respectively to leave that ID unchanged.
Permissions are enforced by the kernel.
.SH RETURN VALUE
Returns zero, or \-1 with errno set.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR fchown (3crunch),
.BR lchown (3crunch),
.BR chown (2)
